# alex — Alex's conversation, permanently.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS ALEX'S CONVERSATION. One DIALOGUE block per npcId across the whole tree, so
# every future Alex quest adds gated nodes HERE rather than starting a second file.
#
# ⚠ IT REGENERATES Assets/Data/Dialogue/Generated/Dialogue_alex.asset, WHICH ALREADY EXISTS AND
# ALREADY WORKS. That asset was hand-authored, was played on 2026-08-16, and is bound BY GUID into
# Prefabs/ModernBritain/Companions/CompanionHome_Alex.prefab. The importer loads-then-mutates, so
# the GUID survives and the prefab keeps resolving — but the asset's contents are replaced
# wholesale by this file every import. Anything you want kept must be written here.
#   - The asset was renamed Dialogue_Alex -> Dialogue_alex on 2026-08-17, GUID intact, precisely so
#     this file's lowercase npcId cannot collide with it. Do not rename it back.
#   - Preset_Alex.Speaker was empty and was set to NPC_Alex the same day. Without it ResolveSpeaker
#     returns null and every line here loses its portrait and name — silently.
#
# THE THREE STATES, gated on rush_hour:
#   not started : he greets you and that is all. No hire offer. (Owner's decision, 2026-08-17.)
#   active      : the Mad Fisherman has sent you. He joins FREE, once, as the worked example.
#   complete    : the ordinary paid hire, £25, from here on.
#
# ⚠ ONE START NODE. A DialogueData has a single StartNodeId, so the opener below is heard in all
# three states and the states are told apart by which CHOICE is gated in. This is the same
# constraint daniel_pauls_quest_one and wtf_mosley live with. It is why "Easy there chap." is the
# opener rather than either of the state-specific greetings.
#
# ⚠ THE FREE HIRE IS RE-TAKEABLE. Hire him free, dismiss him, and while rush_hour is still active
# the free branch is offered again. Accepted deliberately rather than adding a "has ever been
# hired" save field — the cost of the exploit is one companion the quest gives you anyway.

DIALOGUE alex

NODE start
SPEAKER: alex
SPEAK: Easy there chap.
# Pre-quest: a greeting and nothing else. Gated not-started rather than left ungated, because an
# ungated choice shows in EVERY state and would sit beside the hire branches.
CHOICE Hey up.
GATE: not-started rush_hour
# During Rush Hour: the same words open the deal.
CHOICE Hey up. -> alex_deal
GATE: active rush_hour
# After Rush Hour: the ordinary paid hire. These two lines are the ones the hand-authored asset
# already carried, kept rather than rewritten.
CHOICE Come with me .. chap
GATE: complete rush_hour
HIRE: alex
CHOICE Nah I'm okay
GATE: complete rush_hour

NODE alex_deal
SPEAKER: alex
SPEAK: Easy there. Fisherman let me know the deal and I'm down to clown. Don't trust the Chinese as far as I can throw them.
CHOICE Very kind of you. -> alex_charge

NODE alex_charge
SPEAKER: alex
SPEAK: I normally charge too aswell so count yourself lucky. Anyone sparks me out though I'm off.
CHOICE .. makes sense. -> alex_future

NODE alex_future
SPEAKER: alex
SPEAK: After your jaunt in the orient if you need a hand in future holla at ya boy. Protein yoghurts ain't cheap.
# No -> : this ends the conversation, and the hire resolves after it closes. 'free' waives
# Companion_alex's PricePounds of 25 for this choice ONLY — the paid branch above is unaffected.
CHOICE Grand, let's go.
HIRE: alex free
